 on.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Detached epic resume launch[/bold #D7AFFF]                                   [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]launch[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]launch: add the leased, detached submission helper that runs `sase bead [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]work <epic_id> --yes-to-all` and reuses an in-flight resume instead of [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]double-launching.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The EpicResume gate kind[/bold #D7AFFF]                                      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]gate[dim] · [dim][/dim]after launch[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]gate: register the EpicResume gate kind end to end — request spec, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]preview, side-effect-free command, trusted response translation, kind [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]validation, adapter routing, and notification classification.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The epic_resume chop and its feature flag[/bold #D7AFFF]                     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]chop[dim] · [dim][/dim]after policy, gate[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]chop: add the checks-lane chop that detects stalled epics, raises and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reconciles one gate per epic behind a beta feature flag, plus its config[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]knobs and schema.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]User-facing documentation[/bold #D7AFFF]                                     [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]docs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after chop[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs: document the gate, the chop, the feature flag, and the config [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]knobs across the notification, AXE, bead, and configuration docs.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_trib